{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1360449-what-do-you-think-of-thousand-years-of-night","id":1360449,"title":"What do you think of Thousand Years of Night?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-11T21:24:33-08:00","id":1360449,"title":"What do you think of Thousand Years of Night?","content":"Do you think it makes Requiem more like Masquerade because it makes elders much more powerful and introduces the idea of Methuselahs?<br /> <br /> Btw a Requiem is a funeral Mass for the dead. Just learned that today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T21:31:40-08:00","id":1360451,"title":"","content":"TYoN didn't introduce the idea of Methuselahs, which first come up by name in Requiem for Rome way back in 2007, and &quot;elders have often had the time and experience to develop unique Devotions&quot; has been a thing for some time as well. Neither of these things are new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T21:48:22-08:00","id":1360454,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I didn\u2019t know that.<br /> <br /> But I heard that in first edition elders were a lot less powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T22:19:26-08:00","id":1360458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1360449-what-do-you-think-of-thousand-years-of-night?p=1360454#post1360454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I heard that in first edition elders were a lot less powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be on the basis of <i>vampires in general</i> being a lot less powerful in First Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T00:03:15-08:00","id":1360466,"title":"","content":"The difference between Elders in Masquerade and Elders in Requiem is less a matter of power (though Requiem Elders are, indeed, far less powerful) and more a matter of Requiem Elders being powerful due to knowledge and experience, whereas Masquerade Elders are given a leg-up via their Generation, even if they don't have experience due to Torpor or what-have-you.<br /> <br /> Put another way, if a Masquerade vampire were Embraced at 5000 BC and immediately placed into Torpor for seven thousand years, they would still have an edge over other vampires when they woke up, due to much higher Generation. A Requiem vampire enduring the same would be no more powerful than a Neonate. Perhaps less so, depending on how well the Torpor dreams prepare them for the massive differences in culture and technology.<br /> <br /> In short, I don't think elaborating on Elders makes the game any more similar to Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T02:54:15-08:00","id":1360480,"title":"","content":"1ed. Kindred are far less powerful compared to 2ed. Kindred in general. That's mean that, yes, 1ed. eleder are much less powerful than 2ed. Elder.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I don't agree Requiem (2ed.) Elder are less powerful than Masquerade ones.<br /> <br /> In general a 4<sup>th</sup> 5<sup>th</sup> dot in a Requiem discipline is already as powerful as a 6<sup>th</sup> \u2013 7<sup>th</sup> dot (and sometime also 8<sup>th</sup>) of a Masquerade discipline.<br /> Some example (I\u2019m not sure the name translation is correct as I have the manual in other language than English):<ul><li>Presence 6 (the fear) is obtained with only Nightmare 2 (just a 2<sup>nd</sup> dot in this case). Presence 2 is a far longer process to obtain the same, instant, effect from Nightmare 2.</li> <li>Presence 6 (The Rage) is obtained with Animalism 4 which is also much more powerful as it can affect all the people in the whole area and also direct the wrath against to a specific subject.</li> <li>Presence 3 is much more limited than Majesty 2+3.</li> <li>Majesty 4+3 allows practically everything.</li> <li>Dominate from Requiem is generally much more effective than Dominate from Masquerade.</li> <li>The 3 physical disciplines are much more powerful than the Masquerade counterpart (with the exception of Velocity maybe, but this is also due to a different mechanic which is not allowing multiple actions).</li> <li>Animalism from Requiem is not even comparable with the one from Masquerade.</li> </ul>Furthermore, with devotion you can transcend every limit. Thinks to Bone of the Mountain or Force of Nature, Juggernaut Gait, which are completely overpowered compared to any 8-9<sup>th</sup> power from Masquerade.<br /> What is true is the Generation / Blood potency gap. After long torpor Blood Potency drops down dramatically while it\u2019s not the case for Generation but still, it\u2019s also true the opposite: a 8<sup>th</sup> Generation vampire, living for thousands of years, will never close the gap with a 6<sup>th</sup>-5<sup>th</sup> generation vampire (unless he commits Diablerie) while this is not true for Requiem.<br /> <br /> I was actually translating some NPC from Costantinopoli's Twilight for a Requiem dark age chronicle and it was pretty simple to convert Michele powers with just basic disciplines or some simple devotion. And Michele is like a Vampire god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-12-2020, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T03:41:39-08:00","id":1360486,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. That clarifies things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T07:55:57-08:00","id":1360517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1360449-what-do-you-think-of-thousand-years-of-night#post1360449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think it makes Requiem more like Masquerade because it makes elders much more powerful and introduces the idea of Methuselahs?<br /> <br /> Btw a Requiem is a funeral Mass for the dead. Just learned that today.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also latin for &quot;peace&quot; or &quot;rest&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[