don't agree Requiem (2ed.) Elder are less powerful than Masquerade ones.<br /> <br /> In general a 4<sup>th</sup> 5<sup>th</sup> dot in a Requiem discipline is already as powerful as a 6<sup>th</sup> \u2013 7<sup>th</sup> dot (and sometime also 8<sup>th</sup>) of a Masquerade discipline.<br /> Some example (I\u2019m not sure the name translation is correct as I have the manual in other language than English):<ul><li>Presence 6 (the fear) is obtained with only Nightmare 2 (just a 2<sup>nd</sup> dot in this case). Presence 2 is a far longer process to obtain the same, instant, effect from Nightmare 2.</li> <li>Presence 6 (The Rage) is obtained with Animalism 4 which is also much more powerful as it can affect all the people in the whole area and also direct the wrath against to a specific subject.</li> <li>Presence 3 is much more limited than Majesty 2+3.</li> <li>Majesty 4+3 allows practically everything.</li> <li>Dominate from Requiem is generally much more effective than Dominate from Masquerade.</li> <li>The 3 physical disciplines are much more powerful than the Masquerade counterpart (with the exception of Velocity maybe, but this is also due to a different mechanic which is not allowing multiple actions).</li> <li>Animalism from Requiem is not even comparable with the one from Masquerade.</li> </ul><br /> Furthermore, with devotion you can transcend every limit. Thinks to Bone of the Mountain or Force of Nature, Juggernaut Gait, which are completely overpowered compared to any 8-9<sup>th</sup> power from Masquerade.<br /> What is true is the Generation / Blood potency gap. After long torpor Blood Potency drops down dramatically while it\u2019s not the case for Generation but still, it\u2019s also true the opposite: a 8<sup>th</sup> Generation vampire, living for thousands of years, will never close the gap with a 6<sup>th</sup>-5<sup>th</sup> generation vampire (unless he commits Diablerie) while this is not true for Requiem.<br /> <br /> I was actually translating some NPC from Costantinopoli's Twilight for a Requiem dark age chronicle and it was pretty simple to convert Michele powers with just basic disciplines or some simple devotion. And Michele is like a Vampire god.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're talking more about Vampire Revised/V20, but there's a bit of irony in that the current edition of Masquerade is a lot closer to that street level, &quot;Disciplines are nifty magic tricks to hunt humans&quot; feel that early VtR1e was always going for.<br /> <br /> It's a mug's game to compare power levels of different game systems...but I do think Requiem vampires <i>in general </i>are tougher than any version of Masquerade Kindred (that isn't a bad thing or a good thing, it's just difference). How the times have changed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T04:10:26-08:00","id":1365692,"title":"","content":"A really dissapointing book. Of all the lost clans only Akhud got a unique Discipline. Julii are Julii, but even then authors could invent something for them. But Pijavica... the most enigmatic and strange clan of all invented in 2e proved to be... just GANGREL with a new clan bane? Are you serious? If you couldn't imagine a whole new Discipline for them why not make a Vicissitude for 2e?<br /> <br /> Then again, what about 6+ Disciplines? Why not imagine something cool and great? Just a bunch of devotions, after SO GREAT Disciplines of 2e Core&amp; Really?<br /> <br /> And no rules for Storyteller to make cool Elder NPCs. No guidelines for how powelful or not should they be.<br /> <br /> On the whole the book looks lazy written. Authors of 1e wrote much more books and developed them much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T04:21:18-08:00","id":1365693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1360449-what-do-you-think-of-thousand-years-of-night?p=1365692#post1365692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A really dissapointing book. Of all the lost clans only Akhud got a unique Discipline. Julii are Julii, but even then authors could invent something for them. But Pijavica... the most enigmatic and strange clan of all invented in 2e proved to be... just GANGREL with a new clan bane? Are you serious? If you couldn't imagine a whole new Discipline for them why not make a Vicissitude for 2e?<br /> <br /> Then again, what about 6+ Disciplines? Why not imagine something cool and great? Just a bunch of devotions, after SO GREAT Disciplines of 2e Core&amp; Really?<br /> <br /> And no rules for Storyteller to make cool Elder NPCs. No guidelines for how powelful or not should they be.<br /> <br /> On the whole the book looks lazy written. Authors of 1e wrote much more books and developed them much better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's called &quot;word count.&quot; I was a little eyebrow-raised by the Pijavica, but frankly, &quot;Discipline bloat,&quot; &quot;6+ dots,&quot; and &quot;seeming inability to notice the 'oh, and this is how Banes mutate once you're an elder'&quot; are not features I missed. In fact, I'm pretty much doing disco on their graves.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I like the fact it also featured more non-elder things, like the Sons of Phobos update or the Inanimorta (probably not the right spelling, but the seeming reincarnations of old Touchstones that do funny things to elder blood). The book is more useful in general than it is for purely elder games, which was probably the right decision. Also, the new Julii Clan Bane is awesome and makes them completely different than the &quot;Venture before Venture&quot; they used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T11:34:53-08:00","id":1365780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1360449-what-do-you-think-of-thousand-years-of-night#post1360449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think it makes Requiem more like Masquerade because it makes elders much more powerful and introduces the idea of Methuselahs?<br /> <br /> Btw a Requiem is a funeral Mass for the dead. Just learned that today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I think it makes Requiem <i>less</i> like Masquerade by showing us that Requiem elder vampires aren't dusty old relics of the past playing the game from the distant shadows, but instead, they try to keep up with the times and keep playing the game from the front lines. That's pretty much the opposite of what elders are like in Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","user":"Tomorrow's Nobody","date":". 02-07-2020, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T19:27:07-08:00","id":1365924,"title":"","content":"@Tomorrow\u2019s Nobody thank you! That totally makes sense.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> why do the Forsaken hate the Pijavica?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T20:54:22-08:00","id":1365934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1360449-what-do-you-think-of-thousand-years-of-night?p=1365924#post1365924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> why do the Forsaken hate the Pijavica?</div> </div> </div> </div>From their introduction in Vampire 2e Core:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Dragon in Slovakia claimed to have studied several specimens of the Pijavica in detail, in the mid-1800s. She captured and grew them in her laboratory. Her sketches reveal grotesque shapes both manifold and multiform. She observed that the quantity and quality of absorbed blood greatly affected the forms the Pijavica took. The Dragon experimented with many types of stimuli and food, getting the most extreme results from werewolf blood. She hypothesized that the lifecycle of the Pijavica was an accelerated, stunted version of what she had observed in some extremely elder Kindred. Unfortunately, proof of her studies no longer exists. Some decades ago, a local pack of werewolves killed the Dragon and destroyed her lab. All that remains is a partial set of her notes, sketches, and the shattered remains of several specimen jars. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T21:50:40-08:00","id":1365940,"title":"","content":"I bet if there's any information left over it's in the hands of the Ivory Claws. They love that stuff.<br /> <br /> Because I've now posted here I'll briefly go over what I thought about Thousand Years of Night. I do not think it made it more like Masquerade. I think avoiding becoming more like Masquerade might have been sort of a problem the book faced. A lot of things players might want to do are things that were done in Masquerade. Make a broad and powerful clan, for instance. Instead it seemed more focused on the singular personal horror angle and the repercussions of being so old, rather than letting players stretch their muscles in the power that comes with that amount of age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-07-2020, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T00:10:46-08:00","id":1366251,"title":"","content":"While i was a tad disappointed with the Pijavica write up; overall I thoroughly enjoyed the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T05:38:42-08:00","id":1366301,"title":"","content":"So the three types of criticism I've seen against 1kYoN is that they made Elders too powerful, not powerful enough, and had a few disappointing Lost Clans. Since the latter is a minor option tangentially related to the focus of the book, it shouldn't be considered a big deal for the overall quality of the book.<br /> <br /> So what about the power levels of Elders in this book? What does Thousand Years of Night introduce that makes Elders more powerful than if you just built them using the core book?<br /> <br /> 1.) Preternatural Skills. If you have 6+ dots in a Skill you can spend a WP to gain some advantages for one turn or action. How good these are is pretty subjective and context dependent. I personally think that substituting the Preternatural Skill for any other in the same category and being able to downgrade an NPC's failure in contested Physical Skill rolls are the two biggest bonuses. The former can effectively make you have 6+ dots in all Skills, and the latter can be absolutely debilitating in combat depending on what the ST deems is a good consequence for dramatic failure in a battle.<br /> <br /> 2.) Devotions. Some of them are pretty powerful. They're basically on tier with Juggernaut's Gait and Force of Nature from the core book, so basically it's just more options consistent with what we already have.<br /> <br /> 3.) Merits. Practiced Puppeteer stands out as it makes it much more difficult for lower characters to contest or resist that character's already maxed Discipline, and it only costs 2 dots as well. That is definitely something that can make an Elder start lording over their lessers.<br /> <br /> 4.) Blood Sorcery. Scapegoat was immediately banned at my table (just like Coil of Ziva from SotC; so once again consistent with what we already have), but other than that they're just high dot rituals.<br /> <br /> 5.) Diablerising mortals. Has a relatively high Humanity prerequisite, grants less then diablerising other Kindred, and the only benefit is that it's much easier to get away with without discovery since Kindred doesn't keep tabs on individual mortals unless they're personally invested in them, and the possibility itself is pretty unknown.<br /> <br /> 6.) Elder Clan Banes. A drawback instead of an advantage. How much of a drawback it is, however, varies between Clans, and depending on the play style of the player/group.<br /> <br /> <br /> So how much does Thousand Years of Night boost Elders? Not that much, tbh. Preternatural Skills and a few Merits is the only thing that actually elevates Elders. Everything else just provides more options for Elder characters without breaking the ceiling set by other VtR 2e books.<br /> <br /> What 1kYoN does bring is a pretty solid guide for how to play Elder characters in the game. It's probably the best of the second edition supplements for VtR, and not only because all the others have been roller-coasters in terms of quality and usability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:32:59-08:00","id":1367045,"title":"","content":"I only skimmed the book, but I found TYoN interesting because of the way it diverged from standard VtR in mood, while still remaining personal. Both in how an elder relates to their history and their current touchstones.<br /> <br /> My minor criticism is that I would have liked a method to build your own conspiracy, with comparable merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T11:11:26-08:00","id":1367263,"title":"","content":"When I first GMed Vampire I thought it was a pity that history was not really taken into account. A vampire is immortal and a chronicle encompassing several centuries would be interesting though a daunting task for a GM. I think that \u201cA thousand year of night\u201d is doing a great job but you have to mix it with Dark Eras and, yes, it\u2019 still a tremendous job for the GM but it shows you the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}